Add Delete through excluding: the CRUD vocabulary complete, the judgment shared

Dev accepted Delete's first design point on 2026-10-14 ("I accept Delete through
excluding, proceed"): Delete names one domain by TypeName and is judged by the same
whole-ontology validation as a Latent, through `excluding`.

Core: `DomainOntology.excluding(typeName)`, the inverse of `including` — a new ontology
without the domain of that name and package (parameters free, as definitions are keyed),
the one it is called on untouched; an unknown name removes nothing. One dyn on an existing
main-corpus type, so parse scope and the loss count do not move.

User: `draco.dreams.user.Delete` derives Request and carries `fix domain draco.TypeName`;
User holds Delete, Latent, Read, Request and Response — the CRUD vocabulary complete.

Editor: a third branch, `case delete draco.dreams.user.Delete [ ... ]` — `owner` through
`presence(accepted.keys.find(namePath ==))`, `provisional = accepted.excluding(delete.domain)`,
`problems = owner.fold([one Problem naming the domain], \d -> judge(rules, provisional))`,
the state swapped only when quiet, the Actual carrying the domain as the ontology held it
(a stub when not owned), the shrunk ontology delivered through the consumer on
acceptance. Three outcomes follow without a new rule: a domain nothing depends on is
removed; a domain another derives from is refused, DerivationResolvable over the whole
result naming the dependent; a domain the ontology does not own is refused with one
Problem. Draco itself cannot be deleted while anything derives from its root, and
acceptance alters nothing running.

THE JUDGMENT IS NOW ONE GLOBAL: `dyn judge [Problem]` in the Editor's `globals` —
parameters `rules Knowledge`, `provisional DomainOntology`; body: the definitions, the
problems buffer, the session, set/insert ×3/fire/close, `fix value problems.toSeq` — the
first globals section on an actor-minting type. It renders as a companion `def`, visible
inside the minted actor by enclosure, and the Latent branch shrank to six lines calling it.
The emitter orders `factory` before `globals`; the authored drake adopted that.

